                <pb facs="0275" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.014G/532</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-13">December 13, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador of Ecuador called to see me this morning.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador stated by instruction of his Government that Ecuador was prepared
                    immediately to enter into a cooperative agreement for defense which would make
                    it possible for this Government to patrol the Galápagos Islands and the
                    Ecuadoran coast line. I suggested that for reasons of convenience the
                    negotiations be conducted here. The Ambassador asked if I would request Minister
                    Long to make that suggestion to the Ecuadoran Government, which I said I would
                    do.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">elles</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
